  "question": {
    "text": "A variable line $L$ passes through the point $(3,5)$ and intersects the positive coordinate axes at the points $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$. The minimum area of the triangle $\\mathrm{OAB}$, where $\\mathrm{O}$ is the origin, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iJDt9",
      "text": "30",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GLT89",
      "text": "25",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "CHjlt",
      "text": "40",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LJhIT",
      "text": "35",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1 \\\\ & \\frac{3}{a}+\\frac{5}{b}=1 \\Rightarrow b=\\frac{5 a}{a-3}, a>3\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/vczTu120S0ym_kemOFBhnpc-16qUoeKlhBnwZuYepPM.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$A=\\frac{1}{2} a b=\\frac{1}{2} a \\frac{5 a}{(a-3)}=\\frac{5}{2} \\cdot \\frac{a^2}{a-3}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{a}^2-9+9}{\\mathrm{a}-3}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\mathrm{a}+3+\\frac{9}{\\mathrm{a}-3}\\right) \\\\ & =\\frac{5}{2}\\left(\\mathrm{a}-3+\\frac{9}{\\mathrm{a}-3}+6\\right) \\geq 30\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
